## 8. Behavior
### 8.x Search criteria + results
- WHEN the user clicks “Search” (`nextButton`) THE SYSTEM SHALL load results into the grid `k4`. [ctl:nextButton, kit:k4]
- WHEN the user clicks “Reset” (`resetButton`) THE SYSTEM SHALL clear the search criteria fields back to empty / optionLabel. [ctl:resetButton, kit:k2, kit:k3]
- WHEN the user toggles “Show Inactives” THEN THE SYSTEM SHALL update the grid results to include/exclude inactive configurations. [kit:k4]
- WHEN the user hovers the refresh icon in the grid pager THEN THE SYSTEM SHALL show tooltip “Refresh” after ~250ms (top). [kit:k4]

### 8.x Create New (Add dialog)
- WHEN the user clicks “Create New” THE SYSTEM SHALL open modal dialog “Add File Transfer Configuration”. [ctl:FileTransferGridAddButton, kit:d1]
- WHEN the user clicks “X”/close on the Add dialog while it has unsaved changes THEN THE SYSTEM SHALL show a confirmation dialog titled “Alert Confirmation” with message “You have made changes that have not been saved. Do you want to continue?” and buttons “Cancel” and “OK”. [kit:d1]

### 8.x View dialog
- WHEN the user opens a row’s View action (legacy: row double-click) THE SYSTEM SHALL open modal dialog “View File Transfer Configuration”. [kit:k4, kit:d2]

